Z||000014||85SE||05-21-2000||11:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>From what I understand, it's not that tough to make a flamethrower.  Just add a spark plug in your exhaust towards the back.  I guess you'd need a switch and some wiring, but I think the theory is that when you turn the juice to the plug it ignites the unburnt exhaust gasses.  Hmmm...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, IIRC correctly, you also need to get your engine to run fat.  Really fat, so that unburned fuel makes it to the muffler.  I guess that more or less precludes having a cat, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I remember this from an old Hot Rod show that I watched a couple of years ago on TNN.  And someone please tell me that there isn't some poor soul going around with an exhaust on his car like that.  Please tell me it was someone with an airbrush and one heck of a sense of humour! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
